{
  "description": "What a return needs before it can be finalized (PRD W6 steps 5–7, D-005, D-051, PRD Q3), and whether an approver may give it. Unless a case says otherwise: the seller is the salesman …f1 (pos.return.create); the original bill's business date is 2026-11-02 and today is 2026-11-12; the tenant's window is 30 days; one returned item whose category has no policy of its own ({}). An item's category may set `returnable: false` or its own `windowDays`. Days are counted between business dates; day 30 is inside a 30-day window. `original: null` is a return without a receipt: no window, but a non-returnable category still counts. Needs, in this order: return_permission (the seller lacks pos.return.create), return_outside_policy (outside the window, or a non-returnable category), no_receipt_return. `approverMay`: whether the approver holds every permission the needs take in this branch (pos.return.create, pos.return.outside_policy, pos.return.no_receipt); null when no approver is given. Staff as in testing/returns.ts.",
